    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=10$ or $x=1000$.\n\nLet $k=\\log_{10}x$ and solve $k^2-4k+3=0$.",
      "worked": "For the logarithm to be defined, $x>0$. Let $k=\\log_{10}x$, so $x=10^k$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}(10^k)^k&=\\frac{(10^k)^4}{1000}\\\\10^{k^2}&=10^{4k-3}\\\\k^2&=4k-3\\\\k^2-4k+3&=0\\\\(k-1)(k-3)&=0\\\\k&=1\\text{ or }3\\\\x&=10\\text{ or }1000.\\end{align*}$$\n\nBoth values satisfy the original equation: for $x=10$, both sides equal $10$; for $x=1000$, both sides equal $10^9$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 58
